# Stack conventions

- **Framework**: Next.js App Router (src/), TypeScript strict
- **UI**: Tailwind CSS v4 + shadcn/ui (`src/components/ui`)
- **Data**: Supabase project `cezwtrsleuubrfmbhosn` (Auth, Postgres, Storage) + Drizzle ORM
- **Client data**: TanStack Query for server-state fetching/mutations
- **Forms**: React Hook Form + Zod
- **i18n**: next-intl with `en`, `fr`, and `es` under `src/app/[locale]`

## Visual system
Follow `.cursor/rules/design-system.mdc` for every UI/form/email change. Tokens live in `src/styles/tokens.css` + `src/lib/design-tokens.ts`. Do not invent parallel field chrome.

## Domain model
- `organizations` — one tenant per consulting firm (SaaS customer).
- `profiles` + `organization_members` — staff users (Supabase Auth: email/password or Google). Roles: **Owner** (same as admin; unique; account contact; only role that can delete the org or transfer ownership), **Admin** (workspace settings, invites, retention), and **Case Manager** (caseload). Transferring ownership demotes the previous owner to admin. Every member can access all org data. Each profile has optional `rep_*` columns for IMM 5476 (per-account representative).
- `people` — lifelong immigration clients (identity + history)
- `immigration_projects` — time-bound engagements (program_family + jurisdiction + status). `representative_user_id` points at the staff profile whose `rep_*` details fill IMM 5476.
- `project_participants` — people linked to a project with roles; soft-unlink via `left_at`
- `project_forms` — IRCC forms on a project to-do (seeded by program; IMM 5476 always included)
- `project_form_answers` — ask-once questionnaire answers (jsonb) per project. PDF fill, IRCC edition watch, and answer quality flags: `.cursor/rules/ircc-forms.mdc` (`src/lib/ircc/`).
- `customer_portal_access` — portal access_code + access_token on a person; passwords in `private.customer_portal_secrets`
- Portal login verification is **server-only** via `verify_customer_portal_login` (service_role). Never call from the browser.
- Client form fill and document upload via `/[locale]/portal` after portal session.
- `booking_settings` — per-staff public booking page (timezone, window, min notice, buffer, accept-bookings, hashed token). Unique `(organization_id, user_id)`.
- `booking_availability_rules` — per-staff recurring weekly open hours. weekday 0 = Sunday.
- `booking_services` — bookable consultation types (title, description, duration, price). Org-wide catalog.
- `booking_appointments` — public bookings; guest PII org-DEK encrypted. Public page `/[locale]/book/[token]` is that staff member’s page (service role after token hash lookup).
- `booking_blocked_times` — per-staff one-off blocked days/ranges.
- Outbound notifications via Resend only (no inbound CRM mail). Replies blocked; footers include consultant or org privacy contact email.
- `google_calendar_connections` + `private.google_calendar_secrets` — per-staff Google Calendar OAuth; also used for Google Meet when that meeting tool is selected.
- `microsoft_calendar_connections` + `private.microsoft_calendar_secrets` — per-staff Outlook / Microsoft 365 OAuth; also used for Teams when that meeting tool is selected.
- `zoom_connections` + `private.zoom_secrets` — per-staff Zoom OAuth for meeting join links only (not a calendar).
- `staff_booking_integrations` — one calendar (`google` | `microsoft`) and one meeting tool (`google_meet` | `teams` | `zoom`) per staff user; they may differ.

## Layout
- `src/app/[locale]/(marketing)` — public pages (landing lives at `[locale]/page` until moved)
- `src/app/[locale]/(app)` — authenticated CRM dashboard: left sidebar + main content (home, projects, people, calendar, services)
- `src/app/[locale]/portal` — customer portal (link + password)
- `src/lib/supabase` — browser/server/middleware clients
- `src/db` — Drizzle schema and DB client
- `messages/` — locale JSON dictionaries

## Product context
Canadian immigration consultant CRM (Dossierly, operated by Les Solutions Yuzu Inc., operating as Yuzu Solutions Inc.). Prefer bilingual UX and firm multi-tenancy with RLS. Primary create flow is one-screen **New project** with inline people.
